Required behaviour.
(a) The loop records a `host.storage` sample through `spawn_host_record`: at its start, and then whenever its latest one is an hour old. The sample is {archive_bytes, archive_files, projects_bytes, projects_files}: the regular files, apparent sizes summed, under `<root>/.transcripts` and under Claude Code's projects directory, as `runtime::claude_projects` resolves it. The control fold takes the record into no table.
(b) `/api/fleet`'s `health.storage`. `free_bytes`, the workspace root's file system, is read at the request. The sizes are read at most every 10 minutes and kept between reads, with `read_at_ms` saying when: the page polls `/api/fleet` every 3 s in every tab, and one walk of the live root (about 35,000 entries) takes about 0.3 s. The fields:
- `archive` {path, bytes, files};
- `projects` {path, bytes, files, before}: `before` is the `projects_files` of the newest sample at least an hour older than `read_at_ms`, null without one, so a drop like 11-12's shows;
- `workspaces` {path, bytes}: the regular files under the root outside `.transcripts` and `.transcripts-progress`;
- `database` {bytes, tables}: `pg_database_size`, and the five largest tables by `pg_total_relation_size`, as [{name, bytes}], largest first;
- `growth_bytes_per_day`: what was appended to the archive, which is its bytes now less the `archive_bytes` of the oldest sample of the last 7 days, over the days between them; null without a sample at least a day old;
- `days_left`: `free_bytes` over `growth_bytes_per_day`, rounded down; null when the growth is null or not above zero.
(c) web/src/resources.ts: `storageView(storage)` gives the card's words:
- `rows` [{name, size, note}]: "Transcript archive" with note "grows about <size> a day", or "not measured yet" without a growth; "Claude Code transcripts" with note "<files> files", plus ", down from <before>" when `before` is more; "Workspaces"; "Database" with note "largest: <table> <size>";
- `lasts`: "about <days> days at the archive's growth", the days grouped en-US; null when `days_left` is null.
A size reads "<n> MB" to one decimal under 1024 MB (1 MB is 1024 * 1024 bytes), and "<n> GB" to one decimal above.
